  "stronger_oracle": {
    "helper": "New ABI-valid native_enabled_clobber_wake seeds every bit of YMM0..15 to zero, makes raw FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE directly, verifies its own complete helper state after syscall, then vzeroupper/returns the actual wake count. No C call intervenes between clobber and wake or wake and helper comparison. No x87/MXCSR/control/callee-saved-GPR state is changed. AVX gate in main dominates worker creation and every helper call.",
    "worker": "Existing additive AVX worker retains distinct nonzero patterns throughout raw FUTEX_WAIT_PRIVATE and verifies every bit after return0; main still requires raw helper wake1. Original accepted SSE2 files remain unchanged.",
    "preemption": "If worker runs between helper seed and its wake syscall, both sides have distinct expected live state and helper validates its state on return too. This avoids relying solely on the timing of the helper clobber relative to queued wait. Normal callers assume no live caller-saved vector values across the helper C ABI.",
    "focused_negative": "After actual helper wake syscall, inject nonzero pattern into helper YMM7 before its comparison. Main observes -98 and prints ENABLED_FAIL stage=futex-wake code=-98; frozen expected stdout includes earlier syscall PASS. This proves helper execution/comparison participates in the oracle. It is boundary injection, not actual kernel fault injection."
  },
